BT 1 0 0 1 0 125 Tm /F3 11 Tf 17 TL .288088 Tw (Public policy is made for a future that cannot be known. This is not a new observation -- it) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.165359 Tw (is embedded in every cost-benefit framework, every regulatory impact assessment, every) Tj T* 0 Tw .474417 Tw (scenario planning exercise conducted since the postwar formalization of policy analysis as) Tj T* 0 Tw .658549 Tw (a discipline. And yet the dominant tools of policy design remain stubbornly deterministic.) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.171883 Tw (They produce point estimates, project single futures, and commit resources to courses of) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.11643 Tw (action on the assumption that the model's central scenario will materialize. When it does) Tj T* 0 Tw .735329 Tw (not -- as it routinely does not -- the response is typically to update the model and commit) Tj T* 0 Tw (again.) Tj T* ET
