BT 1 0 0 1 0 125 Tm /F3 11 Tf 17 TL 24 0 Td 1.510599 Tw (This book argues that the problem is structural, not technical. Deterministic policy) Tj T* 0 Tw -24 0 Td .914899 Tw (design is not merely a consequence of computational limitations or data poverty; it is the) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.640417 Tw (expression of an underlying epistemic stance that treats uncertainty as a temporary) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.334471 Tw (condition to be resolved rather than a permanent feature to be managed. We propose an) Tj T* 0 Tw .545614 Tw (alternative stance, and with it an alternative set of tools: a probabilistic approach to policy) Tj T* 0 Tw .553724 Tw (design in which uncertainty is not a residual but a primary variable, and in which the goal) Tj T* 0 Tw .772892 Tw (of policy analysis is not to eliminate uncertainty but to produce commitments that remain) Tj T* 0 Tw (robust across the range of futures that uncertainty permits.) Tj T* ET
